      "text": "We have $(10x+2)(10x+6)$ is even since it appears as a product of an even number and an even or an odd and even number.\nWe can also rewrite $(10x+2)(10x+6)$ as $10x(2x+3)$ which is also even as its components are divisible by $2 .$\n\nNext, $(5x+5) = 5(x+1)$ which represents a product of a multiple of $5$ and an integer.\n\nTherefore, since the product of all three results in an even integer and satisfies the criteria to share a common factor of $2$, the largest integer that always divides the given expression is \nboxed{20}.",
